# Agent-sent email — always use MVI branding

Any email **you** send on Julie's behalf (Gmail API, Resend, one-off script, carrier/upline paperwork, vendor correspondence) must use the branded MVI shell. Never hand-roll a bare `<html><body>` email.

## Required wrapper

```js
const { wrapResendEmailHtml, signatureBlockEN, signatureBlockES, LOGO_EN, LOGO_ES }
  = require("./lib/resend-email-template");

const inner = bodyHtml + signatureBlockEN();      // signatureBlockES() for Spanish
const html = wrapResendEmailHtml(inner, LOGO_EN); // LOGO_ES for Spanish
```

This gives the logo header, the white rounded card on `#f4f6f8`, and the Julie
Braunsroth / NPN #21695431 / Mejor Vida Insurance LLC footer with phone,
WhatsApp, site, and email.

Easier path when the content is plain text: `buildStaffClientReplyHtml(text, language)`
in `lib/staff-reply-email-body.js` returns `{ html, plainBody }` already wrapped and
signed — use it for both the HTML and plain-text MIME parts.

## Language

- English → `signatureBlockEN()` + `LOGO_EN`
- Spanish → `signatureBlockES()` + `LOGO_ES`

## Still required

- Send **multipart/alternative** (plain text + branded HTML), not HTML only.
- Do not write your own Julie signature; the wrapper supplies it. Strip any
  sign-off the draft already contains (see `stripTrailingSignature`).
- Business / carrier / upline emails get the same branding as client emails.

## Sending

Gmail OAuth from `.env.local` (`GMAIL_CLIENT_ID`, `GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET`,
`GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN`, `GMAIL_FROM_EMAIL`); see `api/staff/send-email.js` for the
raw-MIME builders, including the attachment variant. Delete one-off send scripts
afterward and keep tax/bank PDFs out of the repo.
